Q: How do you get Visual Studio to put the output in the Project folder? A: <p>I know 2 approaches:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Force specify the output path:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;OutputPath&gt;your\output\path\&lt;/OutputPath&gt;
    &lt;AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath&gt;false&lt;/AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath&gt;
    &lt;AppendRuntimeIdentifierToOutputPath&gt;false&lt;/AppendRuntimeIdentifierToOutputPath&gt;
&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>Copy resources to the output path:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;None Update=&quot;data\**&quot;&gt;
        &lt;CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;PreserveNewest&lt;/CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;
    &lt;/None&gt;
    &lt;None Update=&quot;saves\**&quot;&gt;
        &lt;CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;PreserveNewest&lt;/CopyToOutputDirectory&gt;
    &lt;/None&gt;
&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;
</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>
